# panel 214, lane land-214, 2026-10-14 (its provisional resolution; the
# compiler-engineer's shape x3).
#
# SYMPTOM: a header's call of the runtime's `hero_str_len` split over two lines:
# the reader of a call read only the line clang quoted, so the note at the
# runtime's declaration made it the compiler's, *internal error* at exit 2.
#
# FIX: R2: the unit's opening is refused with the groups' headers and compiles
# without them, so the headers are what clang refused, whatever file of the
# compiler's own a note reaches (`cli/opening_told.hero`).

extern "ffi-a-header-s-call-of-the-runtime-over-two-lines-is-told.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function x3_f() -> i32

function main()
    print(x3_f())
